### d5078 *mel-k- to become soft HEAD krishnamurti-pfeiffer
ETYMOLOGY 
SOURCE NOTE Emeneau uses **bēgh-** and **bēl** to fill the previously missing Proto-Dravidian *e > Brahui ē development. SOURCE emeneau1997brahui[p. 441, §2.1]
SOURCE NOTE Emeneau proposes loss of *l/ḷ as the first member of a consonant cluster, parallel to the established loss of rhotics, citing bēgh-, hōgh-, mux, taf-, and the ha- component of ha-tin-. SOURCE emeneau1997brahui[p. 441, §2.2]
SOURCE NOTE The paper reconstructs **bēgh-** from *mel-k-: *m- > b- before a front vowel, *e > ē, and loss of *l in the cluster. A plural-action interpretation of -gh- is explicitly tentative. SOURCE emeneau1997brahui[p. 442, §4]
